Longitudinal financial data confirms that generational turnover systematically alters the relative pricing of financial versus physical assets, creating distinct investment regimes:

```
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                 GENERATIONAL ASSET ROTATION REGIME MODEL                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| High & Awakening (1950–1980): Real Assets, Commodities, Inflation Hedges    |
| Unraveling (1980–2008): Financial Assets, Equities, Disinflationary Duration|
| Crisis Climax (2008–2030+): Return to Real Tangible Assets & Sovereign Debt Reset|
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
